Lesotho Customs and Excise Act 1982 (not held); rates: the SACU common external tariff; SACU Agreement 2002 (as amended 12 April 2013) art. 18 (1) (goods of the Common Customs Area free of customs duties between Member States) and art. 20 (1) (the Council approves the customs duties applied to goods imported into the Common Customs Area) [R4/fetch/gap/sacu_agreement_wb20210517.pdf]; common external tariff: Schedule No. 1 Part 1, 'Rate of Duty' columns General, EU/UK, EFTA, SADC, as printed in South Africa's consolidation dated 2025-04-04 (SARS Legal-LPrim-CE-Sch1P1Chpt1-to-99, Wayback 20250405095800, R4/fetch/gap/za_sch1p1_wb20250405095800.pdf) and Botswana's dated 01.07.2025 (BURS Tariff Volume I, R4/fetch/bw10/tariff_vol1_july2025.pdf): the same rates on every line below

* LS: VAT 15 % used to take the value out of a tax-inclusive price (duty in the VAT base)
* Lines covered: the HS headings listed (rice, sweetened waters and other non-alcoholic drinks, beer, wine, spirits of 2208.20/.30/.40/.60, cigarettes, petrol, distillate fuel, medicaments, cotton T-shirts, smartphones, cars of 1 500-3 000 cm3); any other code is grade C (otherBp -1). A code coarser than the 8-digit spirit lines (e.g. 2208.30) is grade C (the two container sizes differ).
* Specific duties per litre of product (c/li) are read as money per canonical unit (litre); the amounts are cents of the tariff currency.
* An imported line with no origin pays the General rate (the model's convention, mfnIfOriginUnknown); a SACU origin pays nothing (art. 18); EU/UK and EFTA origins pay their column where it is lower.
* The customs value is the price before VAT and duty; where an excise is also inside the price the line should give customsValue (otherwise the value is overstated by the excise).
-/

